## Context

Tracker [[1703]]. Author choice: heavy review.

## Author constraints (2026-09-30, interactive)

- "What we are working towards is a complete system specification. The idea
  is to write it explicit and review the heck out of it before we launch
  extraction."
- "We want something that works first, then M4 will polish."
- "Pragmatic programmer, results-oriented over theoretical purity."
- Conceptual documents name no storage and no presentation (rule set for
  `docs/jetp-fusion.md`, ticket 1701).

So every rule in a spec document carries the milestone that needs it (M2,
M3a, M3b, M4, or later). The M2 and M3 slice is the minimum that produces
correct, traceable results; everything else is tagged M4 or later and is not
built before it.

## Lenses

1. Within-file coherence: contradictions, undefined terms, undecidable rules.
2. Cross-file coherence: every term, rule and pointer agrees; one home per rule.
3. State of the art: PROV, SKOS, IFLA LRM, bitemporal data, record linkage
   and entity resolution, NUSAP and IPCC calibration, LLM-as-judge
   calibration, data-quality frameworks.
4. Relevance to the data held: a paper walkthrough of about 12 real
   documents across countries, types and formats, through collection,
   extraction, fusion, a result and its presentation.
5. Relevance to data to come: M3a discovery, new countries, AEDIST, three
   years of snapshots.
6. Implementation constraints: padme GPUs and the local model, API costs of
   cross-vendor panels, OpenAlex budget, repository file ceiling, DVC, the
   author's attention; and per milestone, whether the M2 and M3 slice is
   sufficient and minimal ("works first, then M4 will polish").
7. Dead angles: what cannot be represented, wrong or lying sources, legal
   and terms of use, natural persons, drift, single points of failure.

Reviewers are pinned below the author model's family or to other vendors;
then one external cross-vendor pass (OpenAI, Mistral) on the assembled spec.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Seven lens reports and one external report, archived under `docs/jetp-spec-review/wave-1/`
- [ ] A findings ledger with one row per finding: lens, file, severity, proposed fix
- [ ] The author has marked every finding fixed, deferred with a reason, or rejected, and the fixes are merged
